  WHAT BLOCKING COSTS, paired on seed (negative = the lesson got weaker)
    w75  - w100  -0.0957 +/- 0.0091  (-10.5 SE)
    w50  - w100  -0.0889 +/- 0.0080  (-11.1 SE)

  WHAT SILENCING RECOVERS, paired on seed (positive = quieting helped)
    w75q - w75   -0.0059 +/- 0.0070  (-0.8 SE)   6% of what blocking cost
    w50q - w50   -0.0137 +/- 0.0073  (-1.9 SE)   15% of what blocking cost

  SILENCING CHANGES NOTHING (-0.8 SE). The cost of confining a lesson is
  NOT the blocked neurons' perturbation -- it is that they are READ at all:
  their rate sits in the centroid's denominator and dilutes the reachable
  range whether they explore or not. `mask-unaffordable`'s first reason is
  refused and its second stands alone.

  THAT IS STILL AN ANSWER ABOUT THE READOUT, and it points at a cheaper
  build than the fly's: what the lesson needs is a SMALLER DENOMINATOR, not
  an independently taught one. A compartment readout would work, and so
  would anything that stops the non-participating half being summed.
